{"title":"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the beginning of day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there is a single bacterium in a petri dish. During each day, each bacterium in the petri dish divides into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> new bacteria, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cca117c11e298720e03826725b6d317e21ef64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> bacteria are added to the petri dish. For example, at the end of day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> bacteria in the petri dish. If, at the end of day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the number of bacteria in the petri dish is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, find the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We compute: \\begin{align*} a+b&amp;\\qquad\\text{bacteria at the end of day 1,}\\\\ a^2+ab+b&amp;\\qquad\\text{bacteria at the end of day 2,}\\\\ a^3+a^2b+ab+b&amp;\\qquad\\text{bacteria at the end of day 3, and}\\\\ a^4+a^3b+a^2b+ab+b&amp;\\qquad\\text{bacteria at the end of day 4.}\\\\ \\end{align*} So,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de7daa36747baeaf1b555b9611202d97b2e9fdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^4+a^3b+a^2b+ab+b\\equiv0\\pmod{48}.\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"20\" />We factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/36873a5cf0c61a1f94472dae8b093ec425be61ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. We must have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c05b8056f27c64c98de9a5b74a22799c5c8ac9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^4+a^3b+a^2b+ab+b\\equiv0\\pmod{16}.\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"20\" />If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d097fef7f55d88ffc04a71916779cab1624e9ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv1\\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a82fd018ea1bb34b6a29c08dd65a4cff7685de2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b+1\\equiv0\\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />, which is impossible. So, we must have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31e46dc726a2547c2090160088bf03fdf6c9f5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\equiv0\\pmod{2}\\implies b\\equiv0\\pmod{16}.\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />Now, from<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51de12719bd555ff1085d787ac25a6c9f90b4973.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^4+a^3b+a^2b+ab+b\\equiv0\\pmod{3},\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"20\" />we have the following possibilities:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258fff50f662d7e91586fbe4066c5fa79fddacfd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\equiv0\\pmod{3}\\implies b\\equiv0\\pmod{3},\\]\" width=\"301\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb9c99f371a1760c95dbb0faee903ce7c10a658.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\equiv1\\pmod{3}\\implies 1+4b\\equiv0\\pmod{3}\\implies b\\equiv2\\pmod{3},\\text{ or}\\]\" width=\"539\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade2c52e4d63c6e4996714257a0060774fa2f538.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\equiv2\\pmod{3}\\implies 16+15b\\equiv0\\pmod{3},\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />which is impossible. If the former, then the we have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/2863a7090a40f0dd1fe25893cd06f4b130a259ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\equiv0\\pmod{6}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad b\\equiv0\\pmod{48}.\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />If the latter, then we have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3dd6c7ea9d1eb1c2de1fd6acd52cc84b0eacfa5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\equiv4\\pmod{6}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad b\\equiv32\\pod{48}.\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"18\" />The former gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac5774472290aeed6e9b51b891d8937b645122d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=6+48=54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"16\" /> while the latter gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b004b6aa6526878b2af13349f87aa50128873eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=4+32=\\boxed{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"169\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022145\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 90/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4267/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24739:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022145 and revision id 280138. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}